#: ../../../reference/interfaces/polkit-agent-interface.md:2
msgid "polkit-agent interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/polkit-agent-interface.md:4
msgid ""
"The `polkit-agent` interface is a low level interface that permits "
"applications to register with the [polkit authorisation manager](https://"
"www.freedesktop.org/software/polkit/docs/latest/polkit.8.html), _polkitd_,  "
"as a polkit agent. It's primarily intended for systems running {ref}`Ubuntu "
"Core <ref-glossary_ubuntu-core>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/polkit-agent-interface.md:6
msgid ""
"This interface enables the higher level {ref}`polkit interface <interfaces-"
"polkit-interface>` to make access control decisions for requests from "
"unprivileged clients."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/polkit-agent-interface.md:9
msgid "Developer details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/polkit-agent-interface.md:11
msgid ""
"**{ref}`Auto-connect <explanation-interfaces-interface-auto-connection>`**: "
"no</br> **{ref}`Super-privileged <reference-operations-interfaces-super-"
"privileged-interfaces>`**: yes</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/polkit-agent-interface.md:11
msgid "</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/polkit-agent-interface.md:14
msgid ""
"This interface primarily intended for systems running Ubuntu Core. This is "
"because polkit agents make use of a _setuid_ executable, `polkit-agent-"
"helper-1`, which uses PAM. Outside of Ubuntu Core, the PAM environment "
"inside the sandbox is unlikely to match that of the host system on classic. "
"The only Ubuntu Core system currently shipping polkitd  is the Ubuntu Core "
"Desktop."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/polkit-agent-interface.md:16
msgid ""
"See https://forum.snapcraft.io/t/proposal-add-polkit-and-polkit-agent-"
"interfaces-to-snapd/23876 for the original interface proposal and reasoning."
msgstr ""

